  "status_text": "We can count the keys that hide a flipped bit by filling in a table with just 16,384 rows. Take 20 rounds and 97-bit keys. That gives 2^97 possible keys. Fix the row, the round constants and the output bit. Flip the key bit 59 places ahead of the output, counting around the ring. To count the keys that leave that output bit unchanged, test fourteen starting bits against four parity conditions. Each qualifying pattern counts for exactly 2^67 keys. Lean checked the counting rule (L-meta-25508).",
